# ── Ava — version control ignore list ───────────────────────────────────────
# Track: source (*.py, *.sh), the agent config kit (agent/), docs, configs.
# Ignore: the venv, large model weights, biometric/voice data, runtime state,
# generated media, vendored binaries, and anything secret.

# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/

# Local secrets & env overrides (see .env.example).
# The glob is deliberately wide: config_mgmt.update_config snapshots .env to
# .env.bak on every config edit, so a bare `.env` entry leaves a copy of every
# secret untracked-but-committable. Keep the example file visible.
.env*
!.env.example
*.secret

# Runtime state / personal data (dirs kept via .gitkeep)
data/*
!data/.gitkeep
logs/*
!logs/.gitkeep

# Log files anywhere (e.g. gpusvc/gpusvc.log)
*.log

# Generated images + uploads (dirs kept via .gitkeep)
media/out/*
!media/out/.gitkeep
media/uploads/*
!media/uploads/.gitkeep

# Large model weights & the biometric voiceprint (re-downloadable / re-enrollable)
models/

# Vendored Piper/espeak binaries (large, platform-specific).
# bin/ava (the portable CLI wrapper) IS tracked.
bin/piper/

# the GPU service runtime user dir (keep gpusvc/extra_model_paths.yaml at the root)
gpusvc/user/

# SearXNG local config holds a secret_key — keep the run script, not the secret
searxng/settings.yml

# Personal voice recordings used for enrollment
enroll/*.m4a
enroll/*.wav
enroll/*.mp3
enroll/*.opus
enroll/*.ogg

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
*.swp

# User config + secrets (portable install). Same reasoning as .env* above:
# settings._write_config snapshots ava.yaml -> ava.yaml.bak on every Setup save
# and writes through a .ava.yaml.*.tmp, and both hold owner.name / owner.location.
ava.yaml*
.ava.yaml.*
/secrets/
# JIT-consent user data (grants + declared tool tiers)
connector_grants.yaml
connector_tools_cache.json

# Private, deployment-specific (not shipped publicly). Entries for specific
# private apps live in .git/info/exclude (local-only) so their names aren't
# published either.
DEV_NOTES.md
docs/dev/
frontend/src/overlay/

# Generated connector artifacts (derived from a connector.yaml by
# `ava connector tools|policies` — regenerated at setup, not source).
agent/mcp_server_connectors/apps/
# The path generated connector tools used to live at, kept ignored on purpose.
# Moving the rule to the line above without leaving this behind un-ignored a
# directory that still held 24 generated files on every existing install, and the
# next broad `git add` committed them — including four private sibling-app names
# that .git/info/private-names exists to keep out of the tracked tree. An ignore
# rule for a path that "should be empty now" costs nothing; assuming it is empty
# cost a leak.
agent/mcp_server_content/connectors/
agent/policies/generated/

# Architecture SSOT manifest + .d2 sources (deployment-specific).
#
# Only security.svg is tracked. It is generated from the manifest's `security`
# block, which describes trust boundaries rather than named deployments, so it
# stays app-agnostic — and its .d2 IS tracked, so a fork can regenerate it.
#
# system.svg / network.svg are NOT tracked: they render the author's actual
# topology (personal device labels and private sibling apps), and because their
# .d2 sources and the manifest are ignored here, a fork could neither regenerate
# nor correct them. The public architecture picture is docs/assets/architecture.svg,
# which is hand-authored, app-agnostic, and tracked with its .d2.
# policy.svg stays local (it embeds install-specific filesystem paths).
agent/docs/architecture.yaml
agent/docs/diagrams/system.d2
agent/docs/diagrams/network.d2
agent/docs/diagrams/policy.d2
agent/docs/diagrams/policy.svg
agent/docs/diagrams/system.svg
agent/docs/diagrams/network.svg

# Architecture MODEL sheets rendered WITH the private overlay merged in
# (`model.py render --private`). The spine-only renders in docs/assets/model/ are
# tracked and fork-neutral; these carry the owner's private connectors and their
# generated per-app tools, so the whole directory is excluded rather than
# individual files — a new sheet appears here whenever the model grows an area,
# and a rule that has to be updated to stay correct is a rule that will not be.
agent/docs/diagrams/model/

gpusvc/extra_model_paths.yaml

# Personal-app overlay (backend MCP servers/skills/policies + facade)
/overlay/

# Brand masters (logo source art). Deliberately OUTSIDE frontend/public/:
# Vite copies public/ verbatim into the TRACKED frontend/dist/, so 3.8 MB of
# source art parked there would be swept into the repo, into the published
# image, and into the service-worker precache on the next `npm run build` —
# and the frontend-dist-drift CI job would fail on the way past.
#
# Unanchored on purpose, so it catches a `brand/` nested anywhere. That is also
# why Ava's own SHIPPED default marks live in frontend/public/assets/marks/ and
# not .../brand/ — this pattern would swallow them, and a file cannot be
# re-included once a parent directory is excluded.
brand/

# Uploaded brand assets ($AVA_HOME/branding/ — Setup → Branding). Anchored,
# unlike `brand/` above, because this is one specific runtime directory rather
# than a name that could legitimately appear nested. Deliberately NOT the same
# folder as `brand/`: AVA_HOME defaults to the code root, so they would collide,
# and "reset to Ava's defaults" clears this one.
/branding/

# Docs site — generated staging + build output
docs-site/docs/
docs-site/site/

# Personal instance connectors (this box's AVA_HOME = repo root). Entries for
# specific PRIVATE apps live in .git/info/exclude (local-only) so their names
# aren't published — see the note above the DEV_NOTES.md block.
#
# Runtime installs of the shipped example apps belong here too: `examples/<id>/`
# is the tracked source, each README's step 2 copies the folder to
# `$AVA_HOME/connectors/<id>`, and on this box AVA_HOME is the repo root — so
# without an entry a stray `git add -A` commits a second copy of the example,
# which then drifts from the one in examples/ and is the version a forker never
# sees. (The shipped template for this one lives in examples/home-assistant/.)
connectors/home-assistant/
.venv-tts/

# Agent/editor runtime config — drives the local-only demo/ harness, so it
# is meaningless (and broken) for anyone else.
.claude/

# Installed by `cd qa/e2e && npm install` (qa/e2e/package.json pins playwright
# + tsx). On this box it may instead be a symlink into the local-only demo/
# tree, which is the other reason never to commit it: that would bake an
# absolute home path into the repo and break every clone.
qa/e2e/node_modules

# Allocation ledger: live cross-process state (lease locks, breaker counters, per-model
# records). Runtime, not source — and committing it would ship one box's leases to every
# clone, where stale records name models that do not exist there.
run/

# arch.py writes architecture.yaml (already ignored above); its backups are noise.
agent/docs/architecture.yaml.bak

# Drop-in allocation drivers ($AVA_HOME/alloc_drivers). Created by
# settings.ensure_dirs(); a forker's own engine adapters live here and are
# theirs, not ours. See docs/ALLOCATION.md.
alloc_drivers/

# ── Architecture model: OWNER-PRIVATE ───────────────────────────────────────
# github.com/JayMTea/Ava is PUBLIC, so anything tracked here is published. The
# owner's decision is that the assembly tree and everything rendered from it are
# for them alone, so the model CONTENT and every VIEW of it stay out of git:
#
#   agent/docs/model/        the spine + the derived snapshot
#   docs/assets/model/       all 17 sheets, the A0 poster, the explorer
#   docs/ARCHITECTURE_MODEL.md   the write-up
#   agent/docs/adr/0006-*    the decision record
#
# Consequence, stated so it is not rediscovered later: the "tracked SSOT, checked
# on a fresh clone" property from ADR-0006 does NOT hold while these are ignored.
# The guards still run here, on this machine, where the model exists.
/agent/docs/model/
/docs/assets/model/
/docs/ARCHITECTURE_MODEL.md
/agent/docs/adr/0006-hierarchical-architecture-model.md
#
# The TOOLING that builds it is ignored too. It is app-agnostic and a fork would
# arguably benefit, but its tests import the model and would fail on a checkout
# that has none — and "publish the tool, not the picture" is a decision to make
# deliberately rather than by leaving files lying around in a public repo.
/ava_bridge/model/
/agent/docs/model.py
/agent/docs/explorer/
/tests/test_model_schema.py
/tests/test_model_overlay.py
/tests/test_model_derived_stable.py
/tests/test_model_sheets.py
/agent/mcp_server_system/architecture/get_model.mjs
# The hook installer invokes model.py, so it goes with it.
/tools/install-hooks.sh
